Using `by_class.entry(label.to_string())` allocates a new `String` on every single iteration (770 times), even when the key already exists in the map. Since there are only 4 possible static labels, we can avoid almost all allocations by querying with `get_mut` first and only allocating when inserting a new key.

```suggestion
        if let Some(count) = by_class.get_mut(label) {
            *count += 1;
        } else {
            by_class.insert(label.to_string(), 1);
        }
```

