The test `default_rule_uses_manifest_default_precision` is currently a vacuous truth. Because the default structural manifest has 100% coverage, there are 0 default/uncovered tensors, meaning the `"<defaults>"` rule plan is never generated. As a result, the `if let Some(default_plan) = ...` block is never executed, and the assertions are skipped. To make this test meaningful, we should clone the manifest and clear its explicit rules to force tensors to fall back to defaults, ensuring the default rule is actually exercised and verified.

```rust
    fn default_rule_uses_manifest_default_precision() {
        let mut m = embedded_grok1_structural_manifest().clone();
        m.preserve.clear();
        m.fp16.clear();
        m.ternary_candidates.clear();

        let config = QuantizationConfig::default();
        let report = DryRunPlanner::plan(&m, &config).expect("plan should succeed");

        let default_plan = report
            .rule_plans
            .iter()
            .find(|p| p.matcher == "<defaults>")
            .expect("default rule should exist when explicit rules are cleared");

        assert!(
            default_plan.kernel_method == "quantize_f32"
                || default_plan.kernel_method == "convert_f32_to_f16_bytes",
            "default rule should use quantize_f32 or convert_f32_to_f16_bytes, got {}",
            default_plan.kernel_method
        );
    }
```
